1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,600
The Drain

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:07,000
[Music]

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,500
Hey Nolik, come help me!
The fan and the computer needs that.

4
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:18,000
Not right now! Me and Tom Thomas
are painting a card for his parents' anniversary.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,500
Oh! Look at you, you must be so tired!
Hi Simka! It's really great you're here.

6
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:27,000
I have a question. 12th anniversary —
is it spelled with an F or is it with a V?

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,030
Uh, you know what, first put down the number 12,
and then put a dash on there, and then a th.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,439
on there and then a th oh right but first i'll change the water i'll be right back

9
00:00:39,359 --> 00:00:41,359
oh mama left her in here

10
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:58,159
whoa oh no what have i done i spoiled my mom and dad's special day where in the bathroom

11
00:00:58,799 --> 00:01:00,759
My mom's ring was lying there,

12
00:01:00,919 --> 00:01:04,959
and I dropped it into the sink, and now it's washed away.

13
00:01:06,159 --> 00:01:07,399
There goes the day!

14
00:01:07,519 --> 00:01:09,359
It didn't wash anywhere!

15
00:01:09,679 --> 00:01:12,239
Don't you know anything about how a drain trap works?

16
00:01:12,359 --> 00:01:13,479
About a what?

17
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,079
A drain trap is a special curved pipe under the sink basin.

18
00:01:20,439 --> 00:01:24,039
Water flows out of the faucet and flows down into the drain trap,

19
00:01:24,159 --> 00:01:26,079
and after that it goes down to the sewer.

20
00:01:26,879 --> 00:01:29,959
But when you turn off the water, not all of it washes away.

21
00:01:30,079 --> 00:01:31,959
Some of it stays down in the drain trap.

22
00:01:32,599 --> 00:01:37,000
It's made that way so the smell from the sewer won't get back into the house.

23
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:40,400
A ring is much heavier than water,

24
00:01:40,519 --> 00:01:43,560
so if you happen to drop it down the drain, it won't wash away.

25
00:01:43,719 --> 00:01:46,039
It will stay at the bottom of the drain trap.

26
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:51,480
Well, that means we still got a chance!

27
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:54,319
Yeah, but how in the world can we get it out of that trap?

28
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:55,599
Who knows?

29
00:01:55,599 --> 00:01:57,159
I don't know how to swim.

30
00:01:57,159 --> 00:01:59,319
Don't worry, it's all under control.

31
00:01:59,599 --> 00:02:00,919
Do you have any thread?

32
00:02:01,159 --> 00:02:02,039
Plenty of it.

33
00:02:02,239 --> 00:02:04,719
Go get it and I'll be back in a flash!

34
00:02:07,959 --> 00:02:09,400
I can't fix it like this.

35
00:02:09,599 --> 00:02:10,799
I need my welder.

36
00:02:11,079 --> 00:02:12,000
Papus!

37
00:02:12,359 --> 00:02:14,959
I need to borrow your pack-o-mat for a little while.

38
00:02:15,199 --> 00:02:18,400
Now that's a coincidence! I need to use it too!

39
00:02:20,719 --> 00:02:23,479
Masiya, then I need to use your pack-o-mat!

40
00:02:24,039 --> 00:02:24,560
What?

41
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:25,800
I'll bring it right back!

42
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:27,240
Hey! Where are you going?

43
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:29,080
Just watch what you're doing, dear!

44
00:02:34,719 --> 00:02:39,560
Just like the name says, Fixies live to help machines and appliances.

45
00:02:39,759 --> 00:02:43,159
But machines are very big and Fixies are very small,

46
00:02:43,159 --> 00:02:45,360
so they can't get by without tools.

47
00:02:45,599 --> 00:02:49,680
Long ago, Fixies worked with just about anything they could find.

48
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:52,080
Little feathers, threads, fins,

49
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:55,120
But now they have backpacks called pack-o-mats.

50
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:58,320
Inside a pack-o-mat are all sorts of tools.

51
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:01,439
Just push the button and the pack-o-mat spins around

52
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:05,439
quickly shooting out a hook, or a magnet, or even a parachute.

53
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:08,320
Every adult Fixie has their own pack-o-mat.

54
00:03:08,439 --> 00:03:12,200
But before children can get them, they have to go to school and study hard,

55
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:15,600
and then pass an exam before they have the rights of a full-fledged Fixie.

56
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:19,200
And it's only after all of that that young Fixies get their own pack-o-mats.

57
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:26,440
And what? You're going down there with just that on?

58
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:27,800
Not just like this!

59
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:32,280
Like this?

60
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:33,920
Yeah, like that!

61
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:37,640
When I tug the thread, pull me up!

62
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:39,920
She was just saying,

63
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,640
when I tug on the thread, you need to pull me up!

64
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:43,480
I got it!

65
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:44,439
He just said,

66
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:45,439
I got it.

67
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,880
And I don't need to repeat what he says.

68
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:50,640
She said she doesn't need me to repeat what you say.

69
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:57,080
[Music]

70
00:04:22,079 --> 00:04:31,959
Simka, Nolik, thank you. You really saved the day.

71
00:04:32,599 --> 00:04:34,120
That's what Simka's for!

72
00:04:34,879 --> 00:04:37,199
I said that's what Fixies are for!

73
00:04:37,279 --> 00:04:39,719
Tom Thomas, who are you talking with in there?

74
00:04:39,959 --> 00:04:41,439
Oh, your mom came back!

75
00:04:44,639 --> 00:04:45,439
No one.

76
00:04:48,799 --> 00:04:50,719
Hey, can you turn back into Fixies?

77
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:52,280
I've got to ask you a question.

78
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:57,800
I forgot. Should I write 12th anniversary with an F or do I write with a V?

79
00:04:58,160 --> 00:04:59,760
Just write the number!

80
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:01,280
You're right!